From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:51:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_brcm: leave frames from another CPU port to the bridge

A b53 switch forwards the frames of a user port only to that port's own
CPU port: with several CPU ports, the port based VLAN of a user port
holds just that one. A frame that arrives through another CPU port was
sent there by a rule that replaced its destination, such as the CFP
redirect that b53 uses for the Northstar flow accelerator. The switch
has not forwarded it to the other ports, so do not set
offload_fwd_mark: the bridge forwards it in software.

Linksys EA6900, with the traps to port 5 of the following b53 patches,
between hosts on lan1 and lan2 of the same bridge: 5 of 5 pings with
TTL 1 answered, and 10 TCP connections closed without a retransmission,
their FIN and RST frames arriving through port 5.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/net/dsa/tag_brcm.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_brcm.c
@@ -187,7 +187,13 @@
 	/* Remove Broadcom tag and update checksum */
 	skb_pull_rcsum(skb, BRCM_TAG_LEN);
 
-	if (likely(!is_link_local_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest)))
+	/* The switch forwards a user port's frames to its own CPU port only.
+	 * One that arrives through another CPU port was redirected there by
+	 * a classification rule instead of being forwarded, so leave it to
+	 * the bridge.
+	 */
+	if (likely(!is_link_local_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest)) &&
+	    likely(dsa_user_to_port(skb->dev)->cpu_dp == dev->dsa_ptr))
 		dsa_default_offload_fwd_mark(skb);
 
 	return skb;
